#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186620878 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6822804-ecb7-5160-a7dd-0916b23b8c29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620582}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186620582} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c814a55-5040-5480-8802-779cce141194" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620659} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54a6e73d-3c6d-56ae-831c-6e02ea3d67de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620193}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186620193} :answer-field/id #uuid "81718804-a8a0-5ce5-88c6-1682ee5f9b54" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620735} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a7fc24c-a5f4-5c00-bb8a-d91f498da5e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620063}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186620063} :answer-field/id #uuid "89dc7fff-9884-5ed4-b9bb-d0208e5abc1f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186620743}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d941eb8d-1bd8-5074-93db-8220b3e9b6b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-220298" :question/problem "Find the set of values of $z$ that satisfy $-18<10+7z<24$ and $3z\\ge -9.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$z<$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "To solve compound \"and\" inequalities, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection.\n\n- First, we solve $-18<10+7z<24\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-18 & <10+7z<24 \\\\ -18-10 & <10+7z-10<24-10 \\\\ -28 & <7z<14 \\\\ \\frac{-28}{7} & <\\frac{7z}{7}<\\frac{14}{7} \\\\ -4 & <z<2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/77/778e9b621c822549cdd15f68553596e6a4a53026588ad9832fdb251e7e851b02.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $3z\\ge -9\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3z & \\ge -9 \\\\ \\frac{3z}{3} & \\ge \\frac{-9}{3} \\\\ z & \\ge -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/ad/ad16a2201986ec6531d6dca654b74ca10f34bf6859e0275aea472364b7262800.png)\n\nTo find the values of $z$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/26/26b85fb5ad553bf0c71c109d5d5aecf318e81c70919be4f8040291ee22c28577.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $-3\\le z<2.$"}]}
